From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: vkd3d-crossover <noreply@vkd3d-crossover.invalid>
Date: Tue, 17 Nov 2026 01:07:40 -0500
Subject: [PATCH 10/20] fix: pass lane id to helper functions using emulated
 derivatives

Problem: compute, mesh and task shaders that use derivatives,
implicit-LOD sampling or LOD queries inside a non-entry function fail to
compile in Metal.

Root cause: the emulated derivatives reference gl_SubgroupInvocationID,
but extract_global_variables_from_function did not add it to the
arguments of the functions that use it.

Fix: add the SIMD lane id builtin to the function's arguments for
derivative, implicit-LOD sample and OpImageQueryLod instructions in
compute-like shaders.

Verified by: vkd3d-proton mesh shader tests 260/260 (see NOTES.md
Finding 11).

Off switch: none.
---
 spirv_msl.cpp | 19 +++++++++++++++++++
 1 file changed, 19 insertions(+)

diff --git a/spirv_msl.cpp b/spirv_msl.cpp
index a3939a6..f421f15 100644
--- a/spirv_msl.cpp
+++ b/spirv_msl.cpp
@@ -2296,6 +2296,25 @@ void CompilerMSL::extract_global_variables_from_function(uint32_t func_id, std::
 					added_arg_ids.insert(builtin_subgroup_invocation_id_id);
 				break;
 
+			// Emulated compute/mesh/task derivatives (and implicit-LOD sampling / LOD queries built on them)
+			// need the SIMD lane id inside whatever function uses them.
+			case OpDPdx:
+			case OpDPdxFine:
+			case OpDPdxCoarse:
+			case OpDPdy:
+			case OpDPdyFine:
+			case OpDPdyCoarse:
+			case OpFwidth:
+			case OpFwidthFine:
+			case OpFwidthCoarse:
+			case OpImageSampleImplicitLod:
+			case OpImageSampleProjImplicitLod:
+			case OpImageSparseSampleImplicitLod:
+			case OpImageQueryLod:
+				if (is_compute_like_shader() && builtin_subgroup_invocation_id_id)
+					added_arg_ids.insert(builtin_subgroup_invocation_id_id);
+				break;
+
 			case OpDemoteToHelperInvocation:
 				if (needs_manual_helper_invocation_updates() && needs_helper_invocation)
 					added_arg_ids.insert(builtin_helper_invocation_id);
